# CLI conventions

The MVP CLI is `packages/cli`. The command surface is in `REALIGNMENT-PLAN.md` ("CLI") and
`realignment/spec/10-cli.md`. There are no generated per-capability commands.

## User-facing tokens are kebab-case

Anything a user types as a name follows **kebab-case**, the same family as enum and union
literals in `typescript.mdc`. TypeScript field names stay camelCase; the CLI is a separate
surface.

- **Long flags:** kebab-case (`--no-start-host`, `--out`). Never camelCase or snake_case.
- **Subcommand and topic segments:** kebab-case.
- **Closed-set flag values:** use the same kebab-case literals as the type union.
- **Short flags:** single letters, only where clearly useful, and never colliding with oclif's
  own (`-h`).

Free-form values (paths, ids, URLs, secret keys) are not renamed.

## Target command surface

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `ecp retrieve`, `ecp execute`, `ecp commit` | The three operations, same inputs and outputs as the MCP tools and the host API |
| `ecp mcp start` | The MCP relay (stdio) |
| `ecp app [path \| id]` | The App on the host API |
| `ecp host start \| stop \| status \| restart \| logs` | The background host (supervisor + HTTP API). `restart` drains and respawns the host to re-read plugins and config; **`reload` is an oclif alias of `restart`**, not a separate command |
| `ecp plugins install \| uninstall \| link \| update \| reset` | ECP-owned plugin management (oclif plugin-plugins is library-only); writes or checks `ecp.manifest.json` |
| `ecp config secrets set \| unset \| list` | Secret values in the local secrets provider; `list` shows keys only |

- **No per-capability commands.** Capabilities are reached through `ecp execute` (a one-step
  execution), not `ecp <plugin> <capability>`.
- **One path per concern.** Don't add parallel command trees for the same thing. Rename in
  place when terminology changes.
- Don't add commands beyond this table without a plan or phase-doc change.

## Input

- **Flags only for top-level primitives.** Nested input goes in `--input <json | file>`, never
  in dotted or repeated flags (model output in flags is too loose).
- Plugin install names are short: `ecp plugins install jsonata` resolves to
  `@executioncontrolprotocol/plugin-jsonata` (scope + `plugin-` prefix).

## Output

- **`--json`** on every command prints `{ ok: true, data }` or
  `{ ok: false, error: { code, message, path, suggestions } }`. Error codes are `ECP_*`
  (catalogue in `realignment/spec/06-operations.md`).
- `--out <file>` writes large results to a file and prints a summary, so agents choose what
  enters their context.
- **Exit codes:** `0` success, `1` execution failed, `2` validation or usage error, `3` missing
  plugins, `4` host unavailable or unauthorized (`realignment/spec/06-operations.md`). Full command
  list and flags: `realignment/spec/10-cli.md`.
- Missing capability or plugin: name the plugin and the exact install command
  (`ECP_PLUGINS_MISSING`).

## Verbs

| Verb | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `list` | Many items |
| `show` | One item in detail |
| `set` / `unset` | Secret values |
| Domain verbs | `retrieve`, `execute`, `commit`, `start`, `stop`, `status`, `restart`, `install`, `uninstall`, `link` |
